# Files that have no business being on the public site.
#
# Vercel deploys the whole repo as static files by default, so every one of these used to answer
# 200 on hometongue.me: the PRDs, the eval harness, the candidate clip lists, the database schema,
# the dev server. None of it is secret (the repo is public and no key has ever been committed) but
# none of it belongs on the product's domain either.
#
# This is an upload filter, not a robots rule. The files are never sent to Vercel at all, so they
# 404 instead of politely asking crawlers to look away. A robots.txt listing these paths would have
# done the opposite of the job: it would publish the exact list of things worth looking at.
#
# Verified before excluding: nothing at runtime reads any of these. api/*.js import only from
# ./ and node:, and the only paths the frontend ever fetches are /api/* and /sw.js.
# Do NOT add js/, css/, clips/, vendor/ or assets/ here — those are the site.

# research, measurement and curation records
data/
tools/
test-audio/

# planning docs and the database schema
docs/
supabase/
*.md

# local-only dev server; production runs the api/ functions on Vercel
dev-server.js
.env.example

# developer tooling config. Vercel already withholds package.json, vercel.json and dotfiles, but
# it serves these two, so they have to be named. Checked by hand after the first pass: eslint's
# config and the editor's launch config were both answering 200 on the product domain.
eslint.config.js
.claude/
